course: dictionary
lesson: 1723
title: Citizenship: belonging to a community
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Citizenship is a noun. It means belonging to a country, with its rights and duties. It also means behaving well as a member of a community.
explain: Use context to find the meaning. «After living legally in a country for some years and passing tests, immigrants can become citizens with the right to vote» tells you citizenship is about being a legal member of a country, with rights like voting.
explain: Now test your meaning. «The rule is one person, one vote, decided by things like age and citizenship.» Swap in your meaning: a person's legal membership of a country helps decide whether they can vote. That makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Citizenship means being a legal member of a country, with its rights and duties.
fact: Good citizenship means helping others, voting, and obeying the laws.
fact: Citizenship is also a school subject about laws, rights, democracy and community.
fact: Dual citizenship means being a citizen of two countries at the same time.
fact: Many countries hold citizenship ceremonies, where new citizens take an oath.
exercise: «Being famous or rich does not give you a vote.» What decides who can vote? | *Things like age and citizenship | Having lots of friends | Being famous | Being rich
exercise: Which phrase is an example of good citizenship? | *Helping neighbours and voting | Shouting at people who disagree | Ignoring the laws | Breaking rules at school
exercise: What does dual citizenship mean? | *Being a citizen of two countries | Being very old | Being on two sports teams | Having two houses
test: According to «After living legally in a country for some years and passing tests, immigrants can become citizens», what must an immigrant do? | Learn to swim | *Live legally there for some years and pass tests | Be famous | Own a big house
test: Which of these is NOT a way to show good citizenship? | *Breaking the laws | Obeying the laws | Helping others | Voting
exam: Choose the best meaning of citizenship: | Having a pet | Winning a race | Being very tall | *Being a legal member of a country, with its rights and duties
